t should enter **Edit Vertex** mode by default, or at least not switch back to **Add Vertex** mode when the avoidance radius is greater than 0.\nNot every obstacle needs vertices, some of them only use the avoidance radius.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a `NavigationObstacle3D` node.\n2. Try dragging a movement axis (cannot move).\n3. Switch to **Edit Vertices** mode in the toolbar.\n4. Try dragging a movement axis again (works).\n5. Deselect and reselect the node.\n6. Try dragging a movement axis again (does not work).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121646/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121646/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}